---
/**
 * /service-areas/ — the areas hub.
 *
 * A separate top-level page from /services/, and linked from the homepage
 * alongside it. This is the directory of WHERE: every area the studio
 * serves, and every service available to clients travelling from it. The
 * services pages answer what; these answer from where.
 *
 * It replaced the nine standalone /service-areas/{area}/ pages, which were
 * each a general area page with no service attached. Under the new
 * architecture the service is the entry point — /service-areas/la-jolla/facial/ —
 * and this page is the mesh that makes every one of them reachable.
 *
 * It is also where the ten zero-demand area pages land after their 301,
 * so it lists every served area rather than only the ones with a page.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Reveal from '../../components/Reveal.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import NapBlock from '../../components/NapBlock.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FaqSchema from '../../components/schema/FaqSchema.astro';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import SpeakableSchema from '../../components/schema/SpeakableSchema.astro';
import { areaShells } from '../../data/area-shells';
import { services } from '../../data/services';
import { getServiceAreasForArea } from '../../data/service-areas-index';
import { areaServicePath, areaPath } from '../../config/urls';
import { business } from '../../config/business';
import { CTA_LABEL } from '../../config/nav';
import heroServiceAreasHub from '../../assets/hero-service-areas-hub-san-diego-coverage-map-kiamo.jpg';

/**
 * The areas, grouped by the climate that shapes their skin concern.
 *
 * The grouping is the useful part: a client reading "coastal" learns
 * something a client reading a flat list of nine names does not — that the
 * barrier damage in Encinitas and the pigmentation in Chula Vista come from
 * the same distance from the marine layer, in opposite directions.
 */
const groups = [
  {
    type: 'Coastal & Beach',
    description:
      'Salt water, marine layer UV and year-round outdoor exposure drive the skin concerns here.',
    slugs: ['la-jolla', 'encinitas', 'pacific-beach', 'del-mar'],
  },
  {
    type: 'Inland & East County',
    description:
      'Past the marine layer, UV load is higher and cumulative sun damage is the dominant concern.',
    slugs: ['chula-vista', 'la-mesa', 'carlsbad'],
  },
  {
    type: 'Urban & Central San Diego',
    description: 'Close to the studio — ten to twenty minutes, no freeway required for most.',
    slugs: ['north-park', 'point-loma', 'hillcrest'],
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How far do clients travel to reach the studio?',
    answer:
      'Most clients drive between five and forty-five minutes. North Park and Hillcrest are under ten minutes with no freeway. Pacific Beach, La Mesa and La Jolla are fifteen to twenty minutes. Chula Vista and Del Mar run twenty to twenty-five minutes. Encinitas and Carlsbad are the farthest — roughly thirty to forty minutes on I-5, depending on traffic.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there parking at the studio?',
    answer:
      'Free parking is available on site. You do not need to find street parking or pay for a garage. The studio is by appointment only, so a space is always available when you arrive.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I combine treatments to make one trip from far away worth it?',
    answer:
      'Yes — combining is discussed at the first consultation when it makes clinical sense. A HydraFacial and dermaplaning can share a single appointment. Procell Microchanneling and a Lira peel cannot be layered in one visit. The plan accounts for where you are coming from and how often a round trip is realistic.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to live nearby to get consistent results?',
    answer:
      'No. Clients from Carlsbad, Encinitas and Del Mar complete full corrective courses regularly. The key is scheduling the series as a block at the start rather than booking visit by visit. A three-session microchanneling series placed at four-to-six-week intervals fits into a calendar whether you are ten minutes away or forty.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the first appointment like for someone coming from outside San Diego city?',
    answer:
      'The first visit is a full consultation, skin analysis, and a first treatment — the $249 new-client visit. It takes longer than a follow-up, so it is worth leaving travel margin. After that appointment you will have a clear treatment plan and a sense of how often you need to come in, which makes the drive easier to plan.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which areas have the most clients travelling to the studio?',
    answer:
      'North Park, Pacific Beach and La Jolla send the most clients, followed by Chula Vista and La Mesa. North Park is the closest — three and a half miles with no freeway. Chula Vista sends the most pigmentation and melasma clients, which reflects the inland UV load and skin demographics in that part of the county.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which treatment is right for my area?',
    answer:
      'Each area below lists the treatments with a page for it, and each page opens with what that treatment actually addresses for that area — the barrier damage salt air causes, the inland UV load, the congestion a coastal climate produces. The consultation still decides the modality, but the pages tell you which ones are worth the drive.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you offer mobile facial services in San Diego?',
    answer:
      'No. Mobile services cannot deliver clinical-grade corrective treatment. HydraFacial Syndeo requires a dedicated water line and electrical setup. Procell Microchanneling requires a sterile environment for post-treatment protocol. DMK Enzyme Therapy requires temperature control and a stable surface. Medical-grade LED therapy requires professional panels, not handheld consumer devices. Mobile facials offer convenience but compromise equipment quality, sterile conditions, and corrective capability.',
  },
];

/**
 * The matrix.
 *
 * Each area, and under it every service with a page for it. This is the crawl
 * path into the cluster — every one of the twenty-five service-and-city
 * pages is one link from here, and every one is also reachable from its
 * service hub and its sibling pages.
 */
const matrix = areaShells.map((shell) => ({
  shell,
  rows: getServiceAreasForArea(shell.slug).map((record) => ({
    record,
    service: services.find((s) => s.slug === record.service),
  })),
}));

/** The areas that have at least one service page. */
const covered = matrix.filter((m) => m.rows.length > 0);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Areas We Serve in San Diego | KIAMO Skin"
  description="KIAMO Skin serves clients from 10 San Diego areas. HydraFacial, peels, dermaplaning, microchanneling and scalp therapy. Find your area."
>
  <BreadcrumbSchema slot="head" trail={[{ name: 'Areas We Serve', path: '/service-areas/' }]} />
  <FaqSchema slot="head" faqs={faqs} />
  <SpeakableSchema slot="head" />

  <article>
    <header class="bg-blush">
      <div class="wrap section-y pt-[calc(60px+72px)] md:pt-[calc(60px+112px)]">
        <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16 lg:gap-20 items-center">
          <div>
            <Breadcrumbs current="Areas We Serve" meta="San Diego County" />
            <h1 class="t-h2 mt-6 max-w-[26ch] text-[2.5rem] md:text-[4rem]">
              Where clients travel from, and what the drive is worth
            </h1>
            <p class="t-body mt-7 text-[1.125rem] max-w-[62ch]">
              One treatment room in San Diego. Clients travel from {areaShells.length} areas across the
              county — from five minutes away to forty — for corrective skin and scalp work performed by
              a California licensed esthetician.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 max-w-[62ch]">
              Every area below lists the treatments with a page for it. Each page opens with what that
              treatment actually addresses for that area, so you can tell whether the drive is worth it
              before you book.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">
              <span>{areaShells.length} areas served</span>
              <span class="text-rose">·</span>
              <span>Licensed Esthetician</span>
              <span class="text-rose">·</span>
              <span>{business.experience} in San Diego</span>
              <span class="text-rose">·</span>
              <span>All skin types</span>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-4">
              <Button href={business.bookingUrl} external>{CTA_LABEL}</Button>
              <a
                href={business.phone.href}
                class="t-body border-b border-ink pb-1 hover:border-rose hover:text-rose"
              >
                {business.phone.display}
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="order-first md:order-last">
            <Image
              src={heroServiceAreasHub}
              alt="San Diego service area coverage map showing KIAMO Skin corrective facial services across the neighborhoods served"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm shadow-lg"
              widths={[400, 600, 800]}
              sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {/* The matrix. The directory of where and what. */}
    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Where you live shapes your skin</p>
        <h2 class="t-h2 mt-5 max-w-[28ch]">
          The skin concern that brings clients from each part of San Diego County
        </h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-6 max-w-[62ch]">
          San Diego is not one climate. Coastal neighborhoods deal with barrier damage and marine-layer
          UV. Inland areas accumulate more UV hours per year and see more melasma. Central San Diego
          clients are close enough to complete a peel series.
        </p>

        {
          groups.map((group) => {
            const areas = matrix.filter((m) => group.slugs.includes(m.shell.slug));
            if (areas.length === 0) return null;
            return (
              <Reveal class="mt-16">
                <h3 class="t-service text-[1.0625rem] text-rose md:text-[1.1875rem]">{group.type}</h3>
                <p class="t-body mt-2 max-w-[56ch] text-ink-soft">{group.description}</p>
                <ul class="mt-8 grid list-none gap-6 p-0 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
                  {areas.map(({ shell, rows }) => (
                    <li class="border border-line bg-porcelain p-7">
                      <p class="t-service text-[1rem]">{shell.name}</p>
                      <p class="t-body mt-2 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">{shell.proximity}</p>

                      <ul class="m-0 mt-5 list-none border-t border-line p-0">
                        {rows.map(({ record, service }) => (
                          <li class="border-b border-line last:border-0">
                            <a
                              href={areaServicePath(record.area, record.service)}
                              class="t-body group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 py-3 transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-rose"
                            >
                              <span>{service?.name ?? record.service}</span>
                              <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">
                                →
                              </span>
                            </a>
                          </li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </Reveal>
            );
          })
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* The trust strip. */}
    <div class="border-y border-line bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap py-10 md:py-12">
        <ul class="grid list-none grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-7 p-0 md:grid-cols-4 md:gap-x-10">
          <li>
            <p class="t-service text-[0.9375rem] md:text-[1rem]">{areaShells.length} areas served</p>
            <p class="t-body mt-1 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">Across San Diego County</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="t-service text-[0.9375rem] md:text-[1rem]">{business.experience} in practice</p>
            <p class="t-body mt-1 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">Corrective skin care</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="t-service text-[0.9375rem] md:text-[1rem]">Licensed esthetician</p>
            <p class="t-body mt-1 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">CA Board of Barbering &amp; Cosmetology</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="t-service text-[0.9375rem] md:text-[1rem]">All skin types</p>
            <p class="t-body mt-1 text-[0.875rem] text-ink-soft">
              Fitzpatrick I-VI, protocols per skin tone
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Every service-and-city page, listed flat. One link from here to each of
        the twenty-five, and each is also reachable from its service hub and
        its sibling pages. */}
    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Every treatment and area</p>
        <h2 class="t-h2 mt-5 max-w-[26ch]">
          All {covered.reduce((n, m) => n + m.rows.length, 0)} service-and-area pages
        </h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-6 max-w-[62ch]">
          Each page covers what that treatment addresses for that area, the honest drive time, and the
          local skin concern. Click through to find yours.
        </p>
        <ul class="m-0 mt-12 grid list-none gap-x-10 gap-y-0 p-0 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {
            covered.map(({ shell, rows }) => (
              <li class="border-b border-line">
                <p class="t-service pt-7 text-[1.0625rem]">{shell.name}</p>
                <ul class="m-0 list-none p-0">
                  {rows.map(({ record, service }) => (
                    <li>
                      <a
                        href={areaServicePath(record.area, record.service)}
                        class="t-body group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 py-3 transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-rose"
                      >
                        <span>{service?.name ?? record.service}</span>
                        <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">
                          →
                        </span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* The FAQ. */}
    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Common questions</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-5">Travelling for a facial in San Diego</h2>
          </Reveal>
          <div class="mt-12">
            <FaqList faqs={faqs} />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-porcelain py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="wrap">
        <NapBlock />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
